#Algorithm

Step 1: Start the program.

Step 2: Create a node structure containing data, left pointer, right pointer, and height.

Step 3: Initialize the root of the AVL tree as NULL.

Step 4: Accept the number of integers from the user.

Step 5: Read the integers one by one and insert them into the AVL tree.

Step 6: Calculate the height and balance factor of each node.

Step 7: If the tree becomes unbalanced, perform the appropriate AVL rotation:
Left-Left (LL) Rotation
Right-Right (RR) Rotation
Left-Right (LR) Rotation
Right-Left (RL) Rotation

Step 8: Perform inorder traversal (Left → Root → Right).

Step 9: Perform preorder traversal (Root → Left → Right).

Step 10: Perform postorder traversal (Left → Right → Root).

Step 11: Perform level-order traversal using a queue.

Step 12: Display the results of all four traversals.

Step 13: Stop the program.
